  "scope": "Causal factor/association/observability diagnosis only; no production changes, fresh perception, independent-drive validation, or full-route replay.",
  "conclusions": [
    "Finite covariance weighting relaxes elongated directions but does not remove partial-center bias or ensure that the weak-direction optimum stays near the prediction.",
    "The new mode removes legacy partial-sign protection and coherent neighborhood direction evidence. Frame 178 benefits strongly when both are restored on identical fixed pairs.",
    "Frame 894 changes two curb targets whose centers differ by more than 4.4 m along the road; the new objective and relative rank threshold jointly permit large longitudinal displacement.",
    "Covariance-rotation and direct shape-gradient terms are small compared with center-position force at reference; disabling those terms does not remove large regressions.",
    "The signed square root of total shape mismatch discards positive Gauss-Newton angular curvature at aligned unequal-scale clouds. A cost/gradient-preserving split corrects this, but changes tested fitted errors by less than 1 micrometer.",
    "The old neighborhood angular information uses engineering scales, not calibrated uncertainty. Diagnostic restorations and rank suppression are not deployed or whole-route improvements."
  ],
